From: GloriousEggroll <gloriouseggroll@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] winepulse: send DualShock 4 speaker audio to Bluetooth controllers.

A Bluetooth DualShock 4 has no USB audio function, so games find no
speaker endpoint for it. When winebus presents the controller as USB
(Steam Input disabled), expose a synthetic stereo 32 kHz endpoint like the
wired one, with the same container ID, and send it to the controller
through hidraw, paced in real time: four SBC frames (32 kHz dual channel,
16 blocks, 8 subbands, loudness, bitpool 25, 112 bytes each) per 16 ms
output report #0x17, using libsbc loaded at runtime. The headset jack state
from the input reports selects the speaker or headset output, and the
speaker and headset volume is set with output report #0x11.

This reuses the Bluetooth DualSense mixer, so several streams on the
endpoint are mixed on one clock. PROTON_DUALSHOCK4_BT_AUDIO=0 disables it.

Packet layout and encoder settings follow DS4Dongle
(https://github.com/snipem/DS4Dongle), whose speaker code is MPL-2.0.
